  "summary_en": "Jordan's bilingual National AI Code of Ethics was issued by the Ministry of Digital Economy and Entrepreneurship under the 2020 Jordan AI Policy. It sets voluntary ethical principles: humanity, inclusiveness and justice, privacy, transparency, accountability, reliability, integrity, and green AI. It also covers the metaverse, ethics in AI research, the risks of non-compliance, and recommendations, including a channel for complaints.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Defines AI and sets eight ethical principles for responsible AI use",
   "Requires explainability, disclosure of accuracy and error rates, and channels where people can get explanations",
   "Requires data to be obtained lawfully and with informed, explicit consent; forbids using AI outputs for defamation or blackmail",
   "Includes principles on the metaverse and on ethics in AI research",
   "The Ministry will run channels to receive AI-ethics complaints and assess harm"
